    "updated_at": "2022-03-29T19:35:32Z",
    "body": "Heya @lexpierce! 👋\r\nI'm totally on board with changing the branch name to `main`. I'm mainly worried about how it'll affect existing PRs and links to code, as well as unknown dependencies. For instance, I think it would break third-party builds and repositories hosting Starship that we don't control. We handle the deployments to Crates, Brew, and Scoop, but there are a dozen others that are maintained by third parties.\r\n\r\nQuestions for other maintainers:\r\n- Is there a good time for us to make this change?\r\n- What other dependencies may exist? Can we prepare for them?",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/starship/starship/issues/comments/1082297782/reactions",
