    "updated_at": "2022-03-29T19:44:19Z",
    "body": "There’s advice from GitHub here: https://github.com/marketplace/actions/default-branch-migration. Also, you can totally change the target branch of PRs by hand with maintainer rights (even if it’ll be a bit annoying with 70 PRs…)\r\n\r\nA good strategy in my opinion, if your really want to make sure nobody’s stuff get broken, is making a release with a warning that the branch will change in the future, and then making the change after another release with a note saying that the default branch has been changed.\r\n\r\nI could notify the owner of the [`starship-git` AUR package](https://aur.archlinux.org/packages/starship-git) on Arch Linux as well, when it’s done.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
